<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 51,036 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 51,036 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 51,036 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Friday, compared to 68,782 tonnes in the same period on Thursday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Friday	   Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 7,639	    7,954</p>
<p>    Import cargo			43,397	   60,828</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, four ships sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours, eight ships were expected to sail and seven were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Palm oil		  9,300	 Vi Vi		  13/6</p>
<p>Palm oil		  4,000	 United Tina	  14/6</p>
<p>Jet A-1 fuel	   25,000	 Al-Badiyah	   14/6</p>
<p>Gas oil		  60,000	 Themera		17/6</p>
<p>Palm oil		  8,000	 Bunga Siantan	22/6</p>
<p>Palm oil		 10,000	 Wawasan Courage     due</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 25,000	 Jaguar		  due</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
